\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{The halved expression, and a drift}
\date{2026-11-12}

\p{Let #{X} have two points and let the single off-diagonal entry
of #{L} be #{1}, over #{\mathbb Z}. \ref{fdip-00PB} gives
#{q_x(e)=1}. The expression
##{\tfrac12\bigl(L(fg)-f\,Lg-g\,Lf\bigr)}
uses a factor #{2^{-1}} that #{\mathbb Z} does not have. The
quadratic form itself does not.}

\p{On the directed three-cycle, give every forward edge weight #{1}
and give the reverse of one edge weight #{2}. At the common
source the two weights on that undirected pair differ by #{-1}.
That difference is the obstruction of \ref{fdip-00PG}.}
